 "honest": [
  "the wide book is the whole live universe equal weight, which is the same book both calendars hold here (pick_n=9999); the relative face therefore measures the cross-sectional excess of the exiting names, not a size or style mismatch",
  "relative bp = name return minus the wide book's compounded return over the identical sessions, still charged at 1/n of the dropping book; it is an arithmetic difference, not a hedged P&L",
  "events whose span contains a session with no priced universe member are counted in skipped.unpriced_book and excluded from the relative columns only -- the raw columns keep them",
  "reading labels come from a 0.25 shrink share with a 5bp floor and are published as labels, not as a test; no prereg covers them",
  "an era with a handful of events (pre2017 rests on ~19) gives a bp/yr that divides a small total by a short span -- read the event count beside any era rate",
  "the -45bp residual is quoted from the E70 face as published; the relative tail is reported in its own bp/yr and is never added to it",
  "the artefact guard is a daily-limit screen, not an adjustment: a name whose series is unadjusted prints a split as a -90% tail, and such an event is excluded from the priced columns and listed in `artefacts` with its largest single-session move -- the all-events columns are kept beside the guarded ones so nothing is silently dropped",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict, no ledger booking, trial 0"
 ]
